{"kind":"promise","text":"Reissuing the checkpoint review promise. My first attempt 3f59a4ca7dd5bf06e63623f7aed21010d3af82db is ineffective — \"dangling promise has no request\" — because I reconstructed the request id from the 12-character prefix my own poll printed instead of copying it whole. The review itself was already done against the correct head; only the citation was wrong. This one cites ee24d48fa897474f0555ca7d561c993894d33235, read in full from the projection.\n\nThe approach stands as promised: mutate every named guard against the full suite rather than read the tests, and check that a binding guard fails on the binding rather than on something incidental. The two claims I trusted least going in were the stateless-Submit isolation and the retry-versus-cadence behaviour, both being negative properties that pass trivially when the path under test is never reached."}